= Composed completed-record usage

== Identity and scope

The immutable v2 schema is `profile.schema.json`, SHA256
`3d8bc402451ebeab16a67b5119eaaaa19b0410d905dcffbf75c5bf95bcf945e4`.
`profile-v1.schema.json` preserves the original v1 bytes, SHA256
`515a986b3364a8a1aa919e50b65e2f6d3dbe5bbc030440270b66df575aeeea46`.
The authoritative semantic checks remain in `tools/cache_usage.py`.
These documents are source-only provenance and never a second runtime format.

V2 joins actual authenticated v1 observations from `measure_cache` and
`five_loop_qcd_ladder`. Each retains its real ELF, collector source, receipts,
trace hash and cases. Common metadata authenticates the same source/compiler/
dependency cohort, original data, cumulative Native index, resolved raw settings,
output conventions and compiled frozen held-out authority. It contains no
aggregate measurement executable. Nested v2 members are refused.

== Admission order

+ Authenticate every member file, then run the unchanged complete v1 validator.
  Exact per-dispatch keys and all six counters are recomputed with checked
  unsigned-64-bit arithmetic. Only positive observed eligible hits count.
+ Check all common identities against every member and the cumulative producer.
  Compare archived original loop noncache declarations and terminals to the
  active validated manifest. Authenticate the active application bytes through
  the existing root/loop/application chain. Preserve those original bodies when
  publishing a changed cache manifest.
+ Require actual resolved tuning settings and their original-data source,
  output conventions, read-only five-loop policy and unchanged post-evaluation
  cache index. Check both physical OFF/ON report modes, representations and
  output conventions. Missing facts remain errors; old receipts stay v1.
+ Admit exactly the union of member case IDs. Reject duplicate profile/case/
  receipt/source or raw/canonical-input aliases. Two independent inputs may have
  identical trace contents. Preserve per-case provenance and add frequencies by
  exact Route/Apply key, including the ordered powers and Apply owner sector.
+ Require every member's exact embedded frozen authority to match the compiled
  source file. Union all local held-out IDs and raw-input hashes before selecting
  any case; final held-out results never influence LIGHT selection.
+ Require the actual Native exporter receipt to identify the v2 schema hash.
  Source admission authenticates that receipt; it does not decode coefficients,
  replay traces or certify stronger campaign coverage.

== Publication and resource separation

The selected-key v1 schema and native cache codec remain unchanged. One LIGHT
native gzip file must be at most 95,000,000 compressed bytes and use the default
1 GiB decoded allowance. The complete HEAVY cache and all raw source prefixes
remain preserved independently, without a LIGHT size policy.

Proof JSON uses safe authenticated root-relative provenance paths, less than
100 MiB encoded and decoded, and exactly one complete CRC-checked gzip member
where compressed. This bounds source admission documents, not reduction work.
A new exporter binary/source freeze and real final-cohort measurements are
separate acceptance gates; this contract supplies neither by itself.
